## Architectural Significance

The Lender Out OS V2 demonstrates that external CRM actions, document communications, and lender assignments can operate as governed extensions of the internal lending lifecycle.

Each external action is authorized by persistent application state, performed within a bounded workflow, and followed by an explicit state update. This prevents external integrations from functioning as opaque endpoints and preserves observability across the boundary between HyperSync and downstream platforms.

